Q1. Create the following tables (Giving names to all the constraints are mandatory).

Answer:

a) Table Name: Client_Master

CREATE TABLE Client_Master (
    Client_no VARCHAR2(5)
        CONSTRAINT pk_client PRIMARY KEY
        CONSTRAINT chk_client_no CHECK (Client_no LIKE 'C%'),

    Name VARCHAR2(20)
        CONSTRAINT nn_client_name NOT NULL
        CONSTRAINT uq_client_name UNIQUE,

    Address1 VARCHAR2(30),
    State VARCHAR2(30),

    City VARCHAR2(15)
        CONSTRAINT chk_city CHECK (City IN ('Delhi', 'Mumbai', 'Chennai'))
);

